      "content": "I would caution against trying to clean and seal the wound yourself, as improper technique can lead to further irritation and increase the risk of infection. Instead, if possible, consider wrapping the injury in a sterile bandage or cloth to protect it until you can visit a clinic. If you must treat it immediately, clean the area with mild soap and water, and apply an over-the-counter antibiotic ointment and a non-stick bandage.",
